# Production Environment Variables Template
# Copy these to your Vercel Dashboard > Settings > Environment Variables

# ==============================================
# REQUIRED: Multi-Admin Authentication
# ==============================================

# Option 1: Multi-Admin Mode (Recommended)
# Copy the ADMIN_USERS value from running: npm run generate-admin-users
ADMIN_USERS='[{"username":"admin","passwordHash":"$2a$12$..."},{"username":"superadmin","passwordHash":"$2a$12$..."}]'

# Option 2: Single Admin Mode (Backward Compatibility)
# ADMIN_PASSWORD_HASH=$2a$12$your-bcrypt-hash-here

# Required: JWT Secret (copy from generate-admin-users output)
JWT_SECRET=your-secure-64-character-secret-here

# ==============================================
# OPTIONAL: Enhanced Features
# ==============================================

# Redis for distributed rate limiting (optional)
# REDIS_URL=redis://user:password@your-redis-host:6379

# Firebase for audit logging (optional)
# FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-firebase-project-id

# External audit webhook (optional)
# AUDIT_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/your/webhook/url

# ==============================================
# DEPLOYMENT NOTES
# ==============================================

# 1. DO NOT commit this file to Git
# 2. Use Vercel Dashboard to set these variables
# 3. Test with your production domain after deployment
# 4. Change default passwords before production use

